    {
      "tag": "SELECT",
      "id": "channel",
      "text": "All six together\nD · Definitions\nR · Reference locations\nT · Call target\nC · Callers\nE · Callees\nP · Position definitions",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "One large block\nA and F share an entry.\nFailed refresh keeps the last turn.",
      "href": "#detail-4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Two smaller blocks\nB and R each get fresh entries.\nRelease clears before it waits.",
      "href": "#detail-5",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Try the return lens\nReference and position projections are fresh.\nTheir underlying locations are reused.",
      "href": "#detail-10",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "TypeScriptBackend\nRefresh succeeds → begin turn\nRelease → await service\nCHANGED: release completion barrier",
      "href": "#detail-5",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "Semantic query service\nDefinitions · reference locations · call target\nCallers · callees · position definitions\nAlgorithms and keys stay here",
      "href": "#detail-2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "TypeScriptProjectGraph\nReleases project resources",
      "href": "#detail-5",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "TurnScopedCacheScope\nbeginTurn / release\n→ synchronously clear all\nD\nR\nT\nC\nE\nP\nCHANGED: generic lifecycle lives here",
      "href": "#detail-1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "",
      "text": "PR states the new barrier; the larger spec asks for unchanged lifecycle outcomes. That tension has no recorded explanation. ↗",
      "href": "#detail-12",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-1",
      "text": "01\nSTATED\nMove the lifetime owner\n\nCore exports the generic scope and cache interface. TypeScript keeps semantic algorithms, key construction and project resources; its service cal",
      "href": "#detail-1",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-2",
      "text": "02\nSTATED\nShare expiry, isolate stores\n\nOne scope owns six typed stores: five promise caches by symbol identity and one location cache by file position. Callers reuse reference dis",
      "href": "#detail-2",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-3",
      "text": "03\nSTATED\nCache “nothing” too\n\nA present key whose value is undefined stays cached. An empty location array stays cached too. Lookup uses Map.has before Map.get.\n\nPR: undefined is ",
      "href": "#detail-3",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-4",
      "text": "04\nSTATED\nCut only after success\n\nSuccessful backend refresh begins the next cache turn. A failed refresh leaves existing query entries available. The refresh ordering already exis",
      "href": "#detail-4",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-5",
      "text": "05\nSTATED\nClear now; finish later\n\nRelease synchronously empties all stores, then awaits project release. Backend completion now waits and receives project rejection. Queries can r",
      "href": "#detail-5",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-6",
      "text": "06\nSTATED\nKeep the exact return\n\nNo promise wrapping or cancellation in the cache: rejected promises stay cached; synchronous factory throws retry. An old pending promise may settl",
      "href": "#detail-6",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-7",
      "text": "07\nUNEXPLAINED\nContain the scope\n\nThe query service creates and contains a TurnScopedCacheScope. The architecture plan describes shared core bases extended by TypeScript; this cach",
      "href": "#detail-7",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-8",
      "text": "08\nUNEXPLAINED\nExpose a manual scope\n\nHandles expose only getOrCreate. Explicit scope calls clear all stores. There is no timer, closed state or handle disposal: stores work before",
      "href": "#detail-8",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-9",
      "text": "09\nUNEXPLAINED\nPass files, not the snapshot\n\nThe exported service’s beginTurn parameter narrows from WorkspaceSnapshot to readonly WorkspaceFile[]. Backend passes snapshot.files. T",
      "href": "#detail-9",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-10",
      "text": "10\nUNEXPLAINED\nReuse locations; project again\n\nLocations cache; reference promises/results and position node arrays are fresh on access. Position nodes are looked up again and can ",
      "href": "#detail-10",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-11",
      "text": "11\nSTATED\nCharacterize before extraction\n\nSix service tests and four core tests are added. The five existing service tests and their assertions remain. Commit order records charact",
      "href": "#detail-11",
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "A",
      "id": "card-12",
      "text": "12\nUNEXPLAINED\nReconcile the release promise\n\nThe PR introduces awaited release; the larger spec promises unchanged lifecycle outcomes. A deferred/rejecting injected graph changes ",
      "href": "#detail-12",
      "visible": true
    },
